.TH XD\-NETCONN 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-netconn \- Network Connections
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-netconn
.YS
.SY xd\-netconn
.B \-\-status
.RI [ interface ]
.YS
.SY xd\-netconn
.B \-\-wireless
.RI [ interface ]
.YS
.SY xd\-netconn
.B \-\-new
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-netconn
is Windows XP's Network Connections (Control Panel), through
NetworkManager: a connection per network adapter, and VPN, broadband and
spare wired connections, grouped as in XP, as tiles or details, with XP's
task pane.
A connection can be enabled or disabled, connected or disconnected,
repaired, renamed and deleted, and its Status, Properties and TCP/IP
settings opened.
.PP
Every change is a NetworkManager call, so NetworkManager's polkit rules
decide what needs a password, which
.BR xd\-polkit (1)
asks for.
Configure and Advanced open
.BR nm\-connection\-editor (1)
when it is installed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-status " [\fIinterface\fR]"
Only the Status of the connection on
.IR interface ,
or of the primary connection.
The network icon of
.BR xd\-shell (1)
opens this.
.TP
.BR \-\-wireless " [\fIinterface\fR]"
Only View Available Wireless Networks.
.TP
.B \-\-new
Only the New Connection Wizard.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nmcli (1),
.BR xd\-wifi\-key (1),
.BR xd\-control (1)
